{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question","id":1224061,"title":"Risen question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-01T20:17:31-07:00","id":1224061,"title":"Risen question","content":"Is it possible for a wraith to become a risen in a body that was not their's? <br /> <br /> Example: Billy learns the required arcanoi, finds a suitable conduit, makes the necessary pact with his shadow, but takes on Jeff's corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T20:19:33-07:00","id":1224270,"title":"","content":"Off of memory, I want to say no. The process and drive behind becoming a Risen is extremely personal and people have a strong tie to their former body because... well it's their body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T23:11:06-07:00","id":1224283,"title":"","content":"Huh. That would make sense. Although I feel like I read somewhere in some supplement that it was possible for it to happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T01:59:22-07:00","id":1224296,"title":"","content":"You don't need to do that. No matter the condition of the body you it can be used to become risen. If I remember it says the body regenerates back to the TOD condition during the process of becoming risen. I will get my book out later and take a look though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23655-copycat","name":"Copycat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T07:46:27-07:00","id":1224363,"title":"","content":"You are right that it regenerates, but there is a limit that is spelled out in the book. For instance, I don't believe that a cremated body can be used","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T17:25:11-07:00","id":1224490,"title":"","content":"In W20 they address shortcuts to becoming Risen which get rid of some limitations, like learning from pro's and things like artifacts. The Post 6th Maelstrom Risen, some do get tossed in other bodies so I hope they at least address it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T04:11:24-07:00","id":1224620,"title":"","content":"Also, in KotE, where the KJ are effectively a type of Risen, you can swap bodies if you're of a certain type. It's pretty much a mixed blessing, as you can assume new identities, but every time you experience the Little Death, you potentially get kicked out of your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T14:15:48-07:00","id":1224805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1224490#post1224490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In W20 they address shortcuts to becoming Risen which get rid of some limitations, like learning from pro's and things like artifacts. The Post 6th Maelstrom Risen, some do get tossed in other bodies so I hope they at least address it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's more of a special situation with the Sixth Great Maelstrom, the Maelstrom throwing scores of wraiths into the Skinlands and turning the Shroud into the near impassable Stormwall rather than a normal thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1224620#post1224620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in KotE, where the KJ are effectively a type of Risen, you can swap bodies if you're of a certain type. It's pretty much a mixed blessing, as you can assume new identities, but every time you experience the Little Death, you potentially get kicked out of your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kuei-jin are quite different from the Risen. Yes, there are similarities but most are cosmetic. What they have is not something the Risen have. In fact, the Kuei-jin can rise from cremated bodies while Risen can't. They need their body to be intact. But while Kuei-jin can only arise within the first two to three months, Risen can rise much later, especially with modern embalming techniques preserving their bodies.<br /> <br /> However, you are correct about the Yulan-jin, an uncommon subspecies of Kuei-jin who's souls are untethered from their bodies. Further there is the KJ Flaw, Different Body, which is just that. You died, were dragged into the Thousand Hells and escaped but ended up returning to the wrong body.<br /> <br /> But that is the Kuei-jin, not the Risen.<br /> <br /> Part of the Risen process requires the wraith going to their gravesite and possessing it which does require Puppetry. Kuei-jin on the other hand is in frantic, desperate state following their escape from the Thousand Hells and aren't really in a cognitive state. Most when they rise are in a feral, mindless state, their raging, frantic P'o in command to further emphasis that point. So it's not out of the question for a Kuei-jin to crawl into the wrong body in that state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T21:29:02-07:00","id":1224885,"title":"","content":"I don't see how that changes anything, it would be nice if it would be addressed in character creation, hence why I mentioned the shortcut section. <br /> <br /> And whoah Wan Kuei can rise from cremation?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T16:28:26-07:00","id":1225761,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Kindred of the East will rise regardless of the condition of their corpse while the Risen require a fairly intact corpse, especially their heart and brain. Without that, they can't become a Risen.<br /> <br /> As for Risen emerging in a different corpse, at the moment there are no rules for that. At least in Wr20. I can't remember if the Risen book brings it up or not but I doubt it. As I've been kind of pointing out, becoming a Risen is a conscious choice, requiring one to go to their corpse and possess it. I can't really any shortcuts to that part of it.<br /> <br /> While again, the wraiths hurling into corpses during the 6GM are a unique situation and not something readily repeatable and if one was going to run game around such wraiths, they would just create the Risen from the get go rather than going through the process with a wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T02:28:03-07:00","id":1226404,"title":"","content":"Thing was it wasn\u2019t just on one day only ghosts were tossed into bodies. The 6th gm was an indefinite thing, and thus the dead were rising wildly nilly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:29:13-07:00","id":1226937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1226404#post1226404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing was it wasn\u2019t just on one day only ghosts were tossed into bodies. The 6th gm was an indefinite thing, and thus the dead were rising wildly nilly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that depends on the gamebook you're holding because the different writers on the other lines had their own ideas on what the 6GM did and it's effects. In Orpheus, the successor to WtO, the 6GM turns the Shroud into the Stormwall that is extremely difficult to pass. Hence why in Orpheus, ghosts older than five or so years that Orpheus starts in post-6GM, are extremely rare. Because wraiths are being created in but never cross the Shroud because they can't and by the same token, older wraiths weren't able to pass through the Stormwall to the Skinlands. It takes a great deal of effort from the specters to finally start tunneling through it.<br /> <br /> Personally when it comes the 6GM, I go with the Orpheus answer since it is the closest thing to a direct continuation on WtO prior to Wr20. And because well Orpheus has been folded into Wr20, further strengthening their ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T11:56:09-07:00","id":1263638,"title":"","content":"i would like to know why in Wr20 the Risen have to travel to the Labyrinth to make a deal with there Shadow. if i remember correctly all wraiths can speak with there Shadows, Hell many can't get them to shut up. so why make you go? if its just to make it more involved to become one, and they seemed to have lost one Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T18:04:30-08:00","id":1266304,"title":"","content":"In the Risen supplement, an alternate body can be taken. I think it's a flaw. I know it was allowed in the past. Wr20 seems to insist heavily in the opposite direction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13097-mrblack83","name":"MrBlack83","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T06:14:52-08:00","id":1266388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1263638#post1263638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i would like to know why in Wr20 the Risen have to travel to the Labyrinth to make a deal with there Shadow. if i remember correctly all wraiths can speak with there Shadows, Hell many can't get them to shut up. so why make you go? if its just to make it more involved to become one, and they seemed to have lost one Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts on this were a) it was done to increase the action/drama, and b) it's more akin to the Kuei-Jin origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T11:37:11-08:00","id":1266464,"title":"","content":"i really enjoyed the DoomSlayers book, but it paints the Labyrinth as near suicidal to go to, becoming a Risen is already not the easiest thing. and now you must go to the Labyrinth to talk to your Shadow, it just seems an unnecessary step. &quot;Adambeyoncelowe&quot; i am not familiar with he origin of the Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:21:24-08:00","id":1266648,"title":"","content":"In a similar vein, is there any way to extend Revivify or use Puppetry on a corpse in some other way? I'd like to create a Death Shedim-like character from In Nomine (they can inhabit corpses)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T13:50:10-08:00","id":1271838,"title":"","content":"craft some new puppetry arts that affect dead bodies in the ways you are looking for, just keep an eye on balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T07:16:52-08:00","id":1271972,"title":"","content":"Potentially a mixed Arcanoi of Puppetry and Inhabit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T08:49:28-08:00","id":1276649,"title":"","content":"Ah, the answer I think. Came across it today from Ends of Empire, p. 149:<br /> <br /> &quot;Persephone (from Risen)<br /> <br /> The oldest of the Risen, Persephone tries to flee into the Skinlands when she receives warnings of the incipient Maelstrom. Her Shadow delays her crossing just long enough, however, and she ends up crossing the Shroud at the precise moment the Maelstrom hits. Some form of resonance ensues, and wraiths by the thousands are blown across the Shroud into the Skinlands. Some possess bodies that are not their own, some return to their own rotting cadavers, and some are simply lost. Chaos, and other, less pleasant things, ensue.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T09:34:32-08:00","id":1276656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1224490#post1224490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In W20 they address shortcuts to becoming Risen which get rid of some limitations, like learning from pro's and things like artifacts. The Post 6th Maelstrom Risen, some do get tossed in other bodies so I hope they at least address it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post 6th Malestrom walking dead aren't risen. Yes, they are Wraiths in dead bodies, but they lack the powers of the Risen and are generally worse off for their condition. If memory serves, they were trying to flee from the Malestrom and got blown into the physical world, at which point they wound up occupying bodies. This essentially created a new &quot;class&quot; of walking dead. Risen would qualify as Hidden (if you use Hunter terms), but I would even suggest that not all Hidden are Risen, if that makes any sense to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T14:16:23-08:00","id":1276691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1276656#post1276656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The post 6th Malestrom walking dead aren't risen. Yes, they are Wraiths in dead bodies, but they lack the powers of the Risen and are generally worse off for their condition. If memory serves, they were trying to flee from the Malestrom and got blown into the physical world, at which point they wound up occupying bodies. This essentially created a new &amp;quot;class&amp;quot; of walking dead. Risen would qualify as Hidden (if you use Hunter terms), but I would even suggest that not all Hidden are Risen, if that makes any sense to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does- Good catch with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T21:13:03-08:00","id":1277993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trategos_Sol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1224061-risen-question?p=1276691#post1276691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does- Good catch with that</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}